function renderLLM(){return header('Work with an LLM, or on your own.','The structured model is the source of the diagrams. Exchange an explicit design context and guarded changes, then review the result here before applying it.')+'<div class="overview-grid"><div class="stack"><section class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / GIVE THE MODEL CONTEXT</div><h2>Export the current design</h2></div></div><div class="panel-body"><p class="muted">Give this JSON file to the LLM with a description of the changes you want. It includes the current model, field guidance, and a change-set template tied to this exact draft.</p><div class="actions" style="margin-top:18px"><button data-action="llm-context" class="primary">Export LLM context</button><button data-action="export-json">Export project JSON</button></div><p class="inline-note">The context includes the structured model and attachment captions; embedded file data is omitted. Exchange project exports separately when the images are needed.</p></div></section><section class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / REVIEW PROPOSED CHANGES</div><h2>Import a change set</h2></div></div><div class="panel-body"><p class="muted">Paste the JSON returned by the LLM or open its change-set file. The project ID and draft fingerprint must match. The complete proposed model is validated before a comparison is shown.</p><textarea id="llm-proposal" aria-label="Proposed LLM change set JSON" style="width:100%;min-height:180px;margin:15px 0;border:1px solid #cbd8cd;border-radius:5px;padding:12px;font:11px var(--mono)" placeholder="{ &quot;format&quot;: &quot;opsdeck-design-changes&quot;, … }"></textarea><div class="actions"><button data-action="preview-proposal" class="primary">Validate & preview</button><label><span class="muted" style="font-size:11px">or open JSON</span> <input id="proposal-file" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" style="max-width:220px;font-size:11px"></label></div></div></section></div><div class="stack"><div class="panel"><div class="panel-body"><div class="eyebrow">One model / two ways to work</div><h2 style="margin:12px 0">Structured, portable, inspectable.</h2><p class="muted" style="font-size:12px">Use forms and diagram tools here, or let a file-capable LLM update a project JSON file and regenerate the HTML with the supplied local command-line tool.</p><div class="option-chip">init → edit → validate → render</div><div class="option-chip">context → proposal → preview → apply</div><p class="inline-note">Guide: design-studio/LLM_GUIDE.md<br>CLI: tools/design_studio.py</p></div></div><div class="notice">Applying a proposal captures a revision before the change and an outcome revision after it. A draft mismatch requires fresh context, so a stale proposal cannot silently replace later edits.</div><div class="notice">This exchange runs offline. Connect your preferred LLM separately; the workspace does not send design data to a provider.</div></div></div>';}
